#### LIVE ARM E: finding #3's race, reproduced with the fix in place ####
# 2026-09-04T01:28:52+08:00
# 2026-09-02 23:36: a sibling kernel took :8000 four seconds BEFORE 'ndt up ovs4' started.
# Here the collision is created AFTER preflight has passed -- the case preflight cannot
# foresee -- so the run reaches stack.sh's [3/3] exactly as it did that night. What must
# differ from 02_ndt_up_failure_leaves_fabric_running.log is what is left behind.

ndt up ovs4
  hosts        4
  topology     setting/StaticNetworkTopologyOVS_10Switches_4Hosts.json
  !!  ports already held before bring-up (yours if a stack is up; otherwise the next
  !!  run measures them). stack.sh refuses at wait_for_port if they are not ours:
  residue: python3 pid 2344945 holding :8080 (tcp)
           -> owner: Ryu's REST API (ryu-manager)
           -> if something else holds it: the kernel pulls topology and paths from the PREVIOUS round's controller
  residue: python3 pid 2344979 holding :6343 (udp)
           -> owner: the kernel's sFlow collector (FlowLinkUsageCollector, SFLOW_PORT)
           -> if something else holds it: the next kernel's bind() fails with `bind() to sFlow port 6343 failed`, and every flow rate and link utilisation then reads zero -- indistinguishable from an idle network
  XX  refusing to build: a port this bring-up needs is held by a process that is
  XX  not part of this checkout's stack (nothing in .test_run/pids/ accounts for it).
  XX    :8080 (tcp) is held by python3 pid 2344945
  XX       should be: Ryu's REST API (ryu-manager)
  XX       if it is not ours: the kernel pulls topology and paths from the PREVIOUS round's controller
  XX    :6343 (udp) is held by python3 pid 2344979
